  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CB01122",
    "sub_id": "45750",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>The three main&nbsp;items of the semester grade&nbsp; are&nbsp; assignments, midterm exam and final term exam with weights&nbsp;30%, 30%&nbsp;and 40%, respectively. The 30% assignments include (5% + 25%).&nbsp;&nbsp;Attendance 5%&nbsp;is used to motivate&nbsp;class attendances and active learning. The final term has 40%&nbsp;because students seem to be more concerned of&nbsp;the risk to have bad grade at the end of the semester. During&nbsp;the midterm exam, some students may not do well as they are facing Statistics course exam for the first time. Assignments will push&nbsp;students to keep reading regularly their notes and&nbsp; textbook. Finally, extra points will be awarded to students who are very active in classroom.</div>\n",
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "Students should avoid all forms of misconducts such refusal to submit the homework, using the mobile to chat or speak  with someone during class, bad manners or shocking behaviors, etc. \n Whenever students want to delay submitting assignments or cannot attend class, they should notify the teacher via email (in English or Chinese). \n\nStudents need to be active and avoid any forms of disturbance during the class hours.  \n\nWhen students fail to abide by the policies, they might suffer consequences: \nFor example, students who do not attend to the classes,   nor  handle their assignments on time for no reason, will get  0 point.\nIn the case of Plagarism and Forgery, the score is  0 point. \nBoth L1 and L2 languages are allowed for emails, discussion and assignments.\n\n學生需要積極參與並避免干擾上課時間。當學生未能遵守規定時，可能會受到後果。例如，無故缺席課堂或未按時完成作業的學生將獲得0分。抄襲行為同樣將被處以0分。電子郵件、討論和作業可以使用L1和L2兩種語言。上課期間拍照和進食通常不是良好的行為。",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div><strong>Integrity of Course Materials:</strong><br />\nI request that you preserve the integrity of the course materials.&nbsp;<br />\nUnder no circumstance should you make public (web postings, social media,etc.) &nbsp;class notes, handouts and other materials that are&nbsp; provided on the&nbsp; website,<br />\nilearn, of this course by the instructor.&nbsp;<br />\n<strong>Academic Honesty:</strong><br />\nAll students taking ( or auditing) this course have, in essence, agreed to the FCU&#39;s Code of Academic Honesty.<br />\n<strong><em>Thus, students should not lie, cheat, steal the words nor ideas of others.</em></strong></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>Brief, Students taking this course should show high level of integrety and honestty in all aspects. Racial, sexual, religious or any forms of discriminations are not allwed in this course.</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>這門課的學生應該在各方面展示高水平的誠信和正直。課程中不允許任何形式的種族、性別、宗教或其他形式的歧視。</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "Y"
  },
